ID: vr-25
Title: Adjustable FaceDot and UniformPolygons density and gaps

Status: DONE
Milestone: More or fewer surface dots/cells with independent visible gaps.
Dependencies: vr-20
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/24

Purpose:
Owner requests control over the number and spacing of dots and polygons.
Use bounded surface-pattern uniforms instead of increasing neural topology.

Tasks:
[x] 25.1 Add per-view density and gap controls with honest sampling semantics.
[x] 25.2 Draw adjustable circular dots and separated rectangular cell outlines.
[x] 25.3 Qualify actual pixels, preserved motion, defaults and bounded cadence.
[x] 25.4 Update guide/book/ledger and sole issue/Project tracking pair.

Acceptance criteria:
Increasing density visibly adds dots/cells; gap changes spacing independently.
Original Claire and FaceMesh remain unchanged; FaceMesh retains mesh detail.
Dots/grid move with the face, remain occluded and do not create a solid surface.
No extra mesh/model/storage allocation per frame or unbounded geometry.

